{#
  The group's search box, shared by the group page and the results page
  so the two can never disagree about where it posts or what it is named.

  A GET form on purpose: a search is a read, its result is a page worth
  linking to and going back to, and a GET carries no CSRF token because
  it changes nothing. `query` is the term already run, refilled so the
  results page shows what produced them.
#}
<form method="get" action="/groups/{{ group.id }}/search" class="d-flex gap-2 mb-3" role="search">
    <label class="visually-hidden" for="group-search-q">Rechercher dans ce groupe</label>
    <input type="search" class="form-control" id="group-search-q" name="q" style="min-height:44px;"
           maxlength="{{ constant('Modules\\Groups\\Support\\SearchTerm::MAX_LENGTH') }}"
           placeholder="Rechercher dans ce groupe…" value="{{ query|default('') }}">
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline-secondary d-flex align-items-center" style="min-height:44px;"
            aria-label="Lancer la recherche">
        <i class="bi bi-search"></i>
    </button>
    {#
      The way back to the whole group, spelled out rather than left to
      "empty the box and submit" — which is what a reader tries first, and
      what used to land them on an empty results page. Only shown once a
      term has actually been run: on the group's own page there is nothing
      to come back from. A plain link, so it works with no JavaScript.
    #}
    {% if query|default('') is not empty %}
        <a href="/groups/{{ group.id }}" class="btn btn-outline-secondary d-flex align-items-center"
           style="min-height:44px;">Tout afficher</a>
    {% endif %}
</form>
